        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Technical review: Document size requirement changes for GPUBuffers mapped at creation]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41560</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41560"/>
        <updated>2025-10-16T14:03:53.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">In Chrome 138, the size requirements for <code class="notranslate">GPUBuffer</code>s mapped at creation have changed. During a <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/GPUDevice/createBuffer" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">GPUDevice.createBuffer()</code></a> call, if <code class="notranslate">mappedAtCreation</code> is set <code class="notranslate">true</code> and <code class="notranslate">size</code> is not a multiple of <code class="notranslate">4</code>, a <code class="notranslate">RangeError</code> exception is thrown.</p>
<p dir="auto">See <a href="https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-138#size_requirement_changes_for_buffers_mapped_at_creation" rel="nofollow">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-138#size_requirement_changes_for_buffers_mapped_at_creation</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds a mention of the change. cc <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/beaufortfrancois/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/beaufortfrancois">@beaufortfrancois</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">Question — if the <code class="notranslate">RangeError</code> is thrown, will an invalid <code class="notranslate">GPUBuffer</code> object still be returned? If not, should I remove the corresponding entry from the validation section?</p>

<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>

<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>



]]></content>
